al":{"m":1752092716770,"key":["I don't want to boombard my readers with a flood of items in the RSS, so I'll keep the aggregate form, rather than splitting them into many snippets, although they may be stored like that in the source code. Another reason is that I don't want to acquire, or suffer from, the instant feedback of posting it like in social media.\n"],"v":4,"parent":"49hkXsk7lOipfgxJW","o":1752478473686,"y":1752478473686,"_id":"265WfUt3buszUwPfa","x":37384,"z":1,"u":1752478473686,"di":[],"typeChildren":[],"ch":[],"kr":[],"vr":[]},"ch":[]},{"val":{"m":1751502992026,"key":["In my opinion, the core of a link blog is to try to ",{"text":"add something extra","i":"m","b":true},", that is to cite and append whatever thoughts ",{"text":"you","i":"m","l":true}," have. They do not have to be deep insights. Nor do you need to stop yourself from digressing. If you agree with the original author, then write down your resonances. If you disagree, then argue against their opinions. If any part recalls your memory or blows your mind, write them down. To me it is not some kind of read-laters (you have to read it first), but a good way to ease your ",{"text":"FOMO","i":"m","iUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fear_of_missing_out"}," — rather than forwarded tens of Hacker News posts, you now act as a news filter for your readers by providing your personal commentary."],"v":4,"parent":"49hkXsk7lOipfgxJW","ai":null,"folderOpen":false,"mh":{"3HH3SZVfdeDWAs0V3":{"m":{"d":1751503245870},",u":1751503245870},"Tey5kfq4br4dGGSll":{"m":{"d":1751504057969},",u":1751504057970}},"o":1752478473298,"y":1752478473298,"_id":"mzxfaSaYejK2Yn5QW","x":36948,"z":1,"u":1752089672382,"ih":null,"di":[],"typeChildren":[],"ch":[],"kr":[],"vr":[]},"ch":[]},{"val":{"m":1751505059718,"key":["Here are some rules:"],"v":4,"parent":"49hkXsk7lOipfgxJW","o":1752478473297,"y":1752478473297,"_id":"hztkO3uEs5hT4NWLn","x":36947,"z":1,"u":1752089672384,"ih":null,"di":[],"typeChildren":[],"ch":["BpbpDExrlYjAwBXjg